<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8244" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεμο-τρεφής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fed by the wind,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.625
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγχος ἀ.</span> a spear from a
			tree <i>reared by the wind,</i> i.e. <i>made tough and strong by
				battling with the wind,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				11.256
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεμοτρεπές</span>
			 or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-στρεφές</span>
			<i>turned,</i> i.e. <i>shaken by the wind,</i>) cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
